  - "Tomita-Takesaki"
  - "beta = alpha sqrt e"
abstract: >
  One self-contained Python file, um.py, whose only runtime input is the digit 1. It derives the
  chain beta = alpha*sqrt(e), materializes and builds an embedded Lean 4 + mathlib kernel (at v409: ladder of
  12187/12187 theorems clean, 34166 audited declarations, axioms in {propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}, zero sorry; the
  previous deposit, v401, had a ladder of 9561/9561 and 29318 audited declarations), runs the
  pre-registered rites of nature, and emits its own bilingual article (PT/EN, PDF and TXT). Quantum
  gravity is PROVED as a logical closure (validity: kernel, pre-registered rites and the GPU system count together);
  confirmation by outside observers (creditation) is refused, and beta_TGL in nature at 5 sigma is pending. The seal
  (um_absoluto_selo.json) is the truth of the repository.
